steodistrofia hereditaria de Albright is a genetic disorder characterized by bone abnormalities and resistance to parathyroid hormone.", "GNAS1:GNAS1 is a gene that encodes the alpha subunit of the G protein that binds to the PTH/PTHrP receptor, playing a crucial role in signal transduction for parathyroid hormone responses.", "OSTEODYSTROFIA HEREDITARIA DE ALBRIGHT:Osteodystrophy is a condition characterized by round faces, short stature, short fourth metacarpal bones, obesity, subcutaneous calcifications, and developmental delay, associated with mutations in GNAS1.", "PSEUDOPSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO:Pseudopseudohypoparathyroidism is a condition where individuals have the phenotype of osteodystrophy but normal serum calcium, phosphate, and PTH levels due to the normal maternal allele.", "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1A:Type 1a pseudohypoparathyroidism is an autosomal dominant condition requiring maternal transmission of the mutation, leading to resistance to hormones coupled with G proteins.", "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1B:Type 1b pseudohypoparathyroidism is characterized by hypocalcemia without the phenotypic anomalies of osteodystrophy, with resistance to PTH confined to the kidney.", "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1C:Type 1c pseudohypoparathyroidism involves mutations affecting G protein coupling to the PTH/PTHrP receptor, leading to resistance to other hormones while maintaining the ability to stimulate adenyl cyclase.", "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2:Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism shows normal AMPc response to PTH but abnormal phosphaturia, lacking the osteodystrophy phenotype and familial characteristics.", "DIAGÉORGE:DiGeorge syndrome is a genetic disorder that can lead to various health issues, including hypoparathyroidism and calcium metabolism disorders.", "HORMONA PARATIROIDEA (PTH):Parathyroid hormone (PTH) is a hormone produced by the parathyroid glands that regulates calcium levels in the blood and bone metabolism.", "HORMONA LUTEINIZANTE:La hormona luteinizante, conocida como LH (luteinizing hormone en inglés), es una hormona producida por la glándula pituitaria. Esta hormona desempeña un papel crucial en la regulación del ciclo menstrual y la ovulación, siendo fundamental para el funcionamiento del sistema reproductivo."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}